{
  "work_package_id": "WP-010",
  "work_package_file": "work/WP-010.md",
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
  "assigned_to": "QA",
  "dependencies": [
    "WP-007",
    "WP-009"
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "When a repository's clone error contains the credential-missing sentinel text (e.g., \"requires a credential for host\"), the workspace detail view shows a \"Missing Credential\" badge instead of a generic error.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The \"Missing Credential\" badge links to the repository detail view (#/repositories/:id) where the user can select a credential.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Non-credential clone errors continue to display as before (no regression in existing error display).",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The credential-missing error detection uses the sentinel text from the error message produced by the orchestrators (WP-007).",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T13:56:12Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T14:09:39Z",
      "duration_ms": 807000,
      "summary": [
        "Implemented credential-missing error display in the workspace detail view across all four acceptance criteria.",
        "Added CREDENTIAL_MISSING_SENTINEL constant ('requires a credential for host') in workspace-detail.js, matching the sentinel text emitted by the orchestrators (WP-007).",
        "Enhanced runSetup() toast logic: when clone failures contain the sentinel text, the toast specifically mentions 'credential errors' and the affected repository IDs; mixed failures show both sets; pure non-credential failures use the original message unchanged.",
        "Added buildMissingCredentialBadge(repoId) helper: renders an <a class='status-badge status-badge-credential'> element with an amber/orange colour scheme (distinct from the red error badge), linking to #/repositories/:id (URL-encoded) for SPA navigation via _router when available.",
        "Updated buildRepoStatusRow() to accept credentialErrorRepoIds (Set<string>): when statusInfo is null and the repo is in the set, the generic 'No data' badge wrapper is replaced with the Missing Credential badge.",
        "Updated buildStatusTableSection() to forward credentialErrorRepoIds to each row builder.",
        "Added credentialErrorRepoIds Set in renderWorkspaceDetail() closure. Added applySetupResultCredentialErrors(setupResult) helper that: (a) adds credential-error repos to the set and immediately updates their badge cell in the DOM, (b) removes repos that succeeded or had non-credential failures from the set.",
        "Applied applySetupResultCredentialErrors() in all three setup call sites: Setup button (onSetupSuccess), Retry Setup button, and health alert onSetup callback.",
        "Added applyStatusMapUpdate() helper replacing the inline polling loops in doPoll() and doRefresh(): clears credential-error flag and calls updateRepoStatusCells() when a repo transitions from no-data to having status data (i.e. successfully re-cloned).",
        "Added CSS: --badge-credential / --badge-credential-bg custom properties in both light (#c2410c / #ffedd5) and dark (#fb923c / #431407) themes; .status-badge-credential rule with hover state.",
        "Added workspace-detail.credential-error.test.mjs with 9 tests covering all 4 ACs plus toast message variants. All 9 tests pass. All 26 pre-existing workspace-detail tests pass. All 55 other view tests pass. TypeScript compiles cleanly."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "gui/public/js/views/workspace-detail.js",
          "gui/public/css/styles.css",
          "gui/public/js/views/workspace-detail.credential-error.test.mjs"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:09:39Z",
          "note": "workspace-detail.js: CREDENTIAL_MISSING_SENTINEL is a module-level string constant. If the orchestrator error message template ever changes, this constant must be updated in sync. A shared constants module (e.g. gui/public/js/utils/constants.js) already exists — consider co-locating this sentinel there alongside STABLE_WS_ID so it is visible to future developers who may not know to look in workspace-detail.js."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:09:39Z",
          "note": "workspace-detail.js buildMissingCredentialBadge(): the badge is an <a> element with both href and a click listener for _router navigation. When _router is null (test or direct-link context), the href still works as a fallback. This is consistent with the pattern used in buildHeaderSection's breadcrumb, so no change needed — just confirming the pattern is intentional."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:09:39Z",
          "note": "workspace-detail.js: The credentialErrorRepoIds Set is populated only from explicit setup() calls (Setup button, Retry Setup, health onSetup). If the page is loaded when a repo already had a credential error from a prior session (i.e. statusMap has no entry for it from page load), the badge will not appear until the next explicit setup run — it cannot be inferred from the statusMap alone. Surfacing this state on page load would require a new API endpoint or persisting the error in the workspace health report. Out of scope for WP-010 but worth noting for future improvement."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T14:10:12Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T14:19:05Z",
      "duration_ms": 533000,
      "summary": [
        "All 9 WP-010 acceptance-criteria tests pass (workspace-detail.credential-error.test.mjs).",
        "All 35 workspace-detail regression tests pass (credential-error + notes + open-button + vscode-button suites).",
        "All other view regression tests pass: dashboard (14), repositories (9), repository-detail (29), settings (17).",
        "CSS variables --badge-credential / --badge-credential-bg defined in both light and dark theme blocks (styles.css lines 48-49, 123-124). .status-badge-credential rule and hover state correctly styled.",
        "Sentinel 'requires a credential for host' in workspace-detail.js matches exactly with both orchestrator source files (workspace-orchestrator.ts, repository-orchestrator.ts) and their compiled dist counterparts — AC4 confirmed at source level.",
        "Edge-case verified: null/undefined error field does not trigger credential badge (typeof guard in applySetupResultCredentialErrors handles non-string errors safely).",
        "Retry Setup and health onSetup paths both call applySetupResultCredentialErrors, ensuring credential badge tracking is consistent across all three setup entry points."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "4/4 AC verified by automated tests",
        "tests_passed": 9,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:19:05Z",
          "note": "T2 (mixed credential + non-credential toast) is exercised implicitly by the toast branching logic in runSetup(), but no dedicated T2 test exists in the test file. The AC1/AC4 mixed-results test confirms the DOM behaviour; a dedicated T2 toast assertion would complete the coverage for all three toast variants."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:19:05Z",
          "note": "The credential badge is only applied after an explicit setup() call. A page reload when a repo already has a credential error from a prior session will show the generic 'No data' badge until the next manual Setup run. This is a known limitation noted by the Developer — out of scope for WP-010 but documented for future work."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:19:05Z",
          "note": "No code changes required — code is clean, well-documented, and consistent with existing patterns in the view."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-06-26T13:56:12Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-06-26T14:19:05Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:09:39Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 4 acceptance criteria are met and verified by 9 automated tests in workspace-detail.credential-error.test.mjs. No regressions in existing tests (26 workspace-detail + 55 other view tests + 73 component/api tests all pass). TypeScript compiles cleanly.",
        "The amber 'Missing Credential' badge (.status-badge-credential) visually distinguishes credential errors from generic red 'No data' errors and links directly to #/repositories/:id for the user to assign a credential.",
        "The sentinel text ('requires a credential for host') exactly matches the orchestrator error messages from WP-007. Any future change to that message template must also update CREDENTIAL_MISSING_SENTINEL in workspace-detail.js.",
        "QA should verify: (a) setup with a HTTPS repo missing a credential shows the amber badge with a correct link, (b) retry setup after assigning the credential clears the badge, (c) non-HTTPS repos (SSH) are not affected."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:19:05Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 4 acceptance criteria verified by automated tests and source-level sentinel comparison. The amber .status-badge-credential badge is correctly styled in both light and dark themes and links to #/repositories/:id with URL-encoding. Non-credential errors are unaffected. The sentinel constant matches the orchestrator error templates (WP-007) exactly. Ready for code review."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

